Notebook[{

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["H_C diagonalisation and the analytic coefficients of H_J", "Title",ExpressionUUID->"5c8fe53e-5e51-495b-ab66-d4390e78eafc"],

Cell["\<\
Per {k,-k} sector of the periodic SSH photonic chain, the capacitive Nambu \
block H_C is diagonalised by  T = T_rot . T_sq :  a phased sublattice \
rotation into alpha_k / beta_k, followed by a two-mode squeeze on each {k,-k} \
pair.  This notebook builds that transform symbolically, checks it \
diagonalises H_C into the bands  Sqrt[1 \[PlusMinus] 2 |\[Delta]_C,k|] , then \
applies the SAME T to the Josephson block H_J and reads off closed forms for \
every coefficient of the transformed  \[Tilde]H_J .  The matrix result is \
cross-checked at the operator level with Q3 (Multiply / NormalOrder / \
Coefficient) and against a stored numerical reference from PeriodicChainSW.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"9c053818-5dfe-44c4-b85a-7195b79a078e"],

Cell["\<\
Fundamental symbols:  ad = |\[Delta]_C,k|  (real, 0 < ad < 1/2),   ph = arg \
\[Delta]_C,k  (real),   dJ = \[Delta]_J,k = g_J1 + g_J2 e^{-ik}  (generic \
complex),   gJ = g_J1 + g_J2  (real).   The -k blocks use the conjugates  \
\[Delta]_C,-k = ad e^{-i ph}  and  \[Delta]_J,-k = Conjugate[dJ].\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"993981e4-01a8-4ab2-83d4-5dbd0b54cc36"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["1  Setup", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"a42aeb4b-5d6a-4504-9c46-76b53de17def"],

Cell["\<\
Needs[\"QuantumMob`Q3`\"];
$Assumptions = ad > 0 && ad < 1/2 && ph \[Element] Reals && gJ \[Element] \
Reals;\
\>", "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[120]:=",ExpressionUUID->"1bcef5dc-17cb-4063-8239-1ea6affbe92c"],

Cell["\<\
dCk  = ad Exp[I ph];                  (* \[Delta]_{C,k}   *)
dCkc = Conjugate[dCk];                (* \[Delta]_{C,-k} = conj  ->  ad \
Exp[-I ph] *)
dJk  = dJ;                            (* \[Delta]_{J,k}  (generic complex) *)
dJkc = Conjugate[dJ];                 (* \[Delta]_{J,-k} = conj *)\
\>", "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[122]:=",ExpressionUUID->"e1375398-8bf5-4272-bcde-75bbb1f9a760"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["2  The sector Nambu matrices (honest 1/2 convention)", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"9b90a75e-4da0-4514-95dc-75a7340ec895"],

Cell["\<\
Basis  (b_{kA}, b_{kB}, b_{-kA}, b_{-kB} ; then the four daggers).  These 8x8 \
blocks are transcribed from PeriodicChainSW.sector_nambu, which is verified \
against the real-space -> k-space Fourier transform.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"21dfb15f-6419-4abb-bcd9-ce872c26ea39"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
sectorFromBloch[on_, bl_] := ArrayFlatten[{
   {{{on, bl}, {Conjugate[bl], on}},        0},
   {0,        {{on, Conjugate[bl]}, {bl, on}}}}];

capNormal  = (1/2) sectorFromBloch[1, dCk];
capPairing = Normal @ SparseArray[
   {{1, 4} -> -dCk/2, {2, 3} -> -dCkc/2, {3, 2} -> -dCkc/2, {4, 1} -> \
-dCk/2}, {4, 4}];
HC = ArrayFlatten[{{capNormal, capPairing}, {Conjugate[capPairing], \
Conjugate[capNormal]}}];

jNormal  = (1/2) sectorFromBloch[gJ, -dJk];
jPairing = Normal @ SparseArray[
   {{1, 3} -> -gJ/2, {1, 4} -> -dJk/2, {2, 3} -> -dJkc/2, {2, 4} -> -gJ/2,
    {3, 1} -> -gJ/2, {3, 2} -> -dJkc/2, {4, 1} -> -dJk/2, {4, 2} -> -gJ/2}, \
{4, 4}];
HJ = ArrayFlatten[{{jNormal, jPairing}, {Conjugate[jPairing], \
Conjugate[jNormal]}}];

MatrixForm /@ {HC, HJ}\
\>", "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[126]:=",ExpressionUUID->"cf974777-c0a2-4aa6-b7ff-04dfa03a491a"],

