Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
7  Comparison against the implemented procedure (PeriodicChainSW)\
\>", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"0cb63d99-e556-4c6b-a4ac-d702d9e8842d"],

Cell["\<\
The closed forms above are checked against the shipped numerical procedure: \
for a set of parameter points, PeriodicChainSW.sector_nambu(k) builds the 8x8 \
blocks and PeriodicChainSW.diagonalize_cap_sector(k) builds the same T = \
T_rot . T_sq, then 2 (T^dagger H_J T) is the physical transformed Josephson \
block.  The points span generic k, the two TRIMs (k = 0, pi), and both \
dimerisation sides (g_c1 > g_c2 and g_c1 < g_c2), all with g_c1 + g_c2 < 1/2. \
 The reference numbers below were produced by that procedure (numpy, \
complex128).\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"317a3a02-b3ec-4a7d-9c31-e3942d9586f3"],

Cell["\<\
reference = {
  <|\"k\"->0.7, \"gc1\"->0.18, \"gc2\"->0.11, \"gJ1\"->1.0, \"gJ2\"->-0.5,
    \"ad\"->0.27347349161566964, \"ph\"->-0.2621166301913443, \
\"dJ\"->(0.6175789063577557 + (0.3221088436188455)*I), \"gJ\"->0.5,
    \"AJnum\"->{{(-0.23606724543142563 + (0.0)*I), (0.0 + \
(0.4310756766297129)*I), (0.0 + (0.0)*I), (0.0 + (0.0)*I)}, {(0.0 + \
(-0.4310756766297129)*I), (1.0881487868209314 + (0.0)*I), (0.0 + (0.0)*I), \
(0.0 + (0.0)*I)}, {(0.0 + (0.0)*I), (0.0 + (0.0)*I), (-0.23606724543142563 + \
(0.0)*I), (0.0 + (-0.4310756766297129)*I)}, {(0.0 + (0.0)*I), (0.0 + \
(0.0)*I), (0.0 + (0.4310756766297129)*I), (1.0881487868209314 + (0.0)*I)}}, \
