Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["8.3  The Zak phase", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"584d7b37-34f8-42c5-a335-117aad36e483"],

Cell["\<\
With abstract real functions beta(k), phi(k) the local Berry connection of \
the lifted spinor collapses to  i \[LeftAngleBracket]\[Psi]_k| \[PartialD]_k \
|\[Psi]_k\[RightAngleBracket] = phi'(k)/2 :  the pseudo-spin angle beta drops \
out of the connection entirely.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"c6f1ab39-d995-46f2-88c5-1b858a3bf31a"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
ClearAll[betaFn, phiFn];
uAf  = {1, Exp[-I phiFn[k]]}/Sqrt[2];
uBf  = {1, -Exp[-I phiFn[k]]}/Sqrt[2];
psiF = I Sin[betaFn[k]/2] Flatten@KroneckerProduct[uAf, {1, 0}] +
           Cos[betaFn[k]/2] Flatten@KroneckerProduct[uBf, {0, 1}];

berryConnection = ComplexExpand[I Conjugate[psiF] . D[psiF, k],
   TargetFunctions -> {Re, Im}] // FullSimplify;
Print[\"i <psi_k| d_k psi_k>  ->  \", berryConnection];   (* -> phiFn'[k]/2 : \
beta drops out *)
Print[\"  minus phiFn'[k]/2 at random functions  ->  \",
  Chop @ N[(berryConnection - Derivative[1][phiFn][k]/2) /.
     {betaFn -> Function[x, 0.7 x + 0.3], phiFn -> Function[x, 1.1 x - 0.2], \
k -> 0.9}]];\
\>", "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[100]:=",ExpressionUUID->"cf017ccd-3bdf-4034-b3e1-481b53fc8448"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 InterpretationBox[
  RowBox[{"\<\"i <psi_k| d_k psi_k>  ->  \"\>", "\[InvisibleSpace]", 
   FractionBox[
    RowBox[{
     SuperscriptBox["phiFn", "\[Prime]",
      MultilineFunction->None], "[", "k", "]"}], "2"]}],
  SequenceForm[
  "i <psi_k| d_k psi_k>  ->  ", Rational[1, 2] 
   Derivative[1][$CellContext`phiFn][$CellContext`k]],
  Editable->False]], "Print",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.997811436621841*^9},
 CellLabel->
  "During evaluation of \
In[100]:=",ExpressionUUID->"1a82cff0-e668-4eef-b972-ef9bbe1cdf80"],

Cell[BoxData[
 InterpretationBox[
  RowBox[{"\<\"  minus phiFn'[k]/2 at random functions  ->  \"\>", "\[InvisibleSpace]",
    "0"}],
  SequenceForm["  minus phiFn'[k]/2 at random functions  ->  ", 0],
  Editable->False]], "Print",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.997811436622922*^9},
 CellLabel->
  "During evaluation of \
In[100]:=",ExpressionUUID->"a6ff1d86-eb22-4ce4-af59-820e682e280f"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]],

Cell["\<\
So the Zak phase splits into an SSH piece and a two-level piece:

  \[Gamma]_Zak = \[Integral]_0^{2\[Pi]} (phi'(k)/2) dk   +   \
(anti-periodicity correction).

The eigenvector  cSpinor = (I Sin[beta_k/2], Cos[beta_k/2])  is ANTI-periodic \
across the BZ whenever the planar vector  (gam rho(k), \[CapitalDelta](k)/2)  \
winds an odd number of times  w_h  about the origin  (beta_k -> beta_k + 2\
\[Pi] w_h) , which adds  \[Pi] w_h .  The smooth piece integrates to -\[Pi] \
w_C  with  w_C  the SSH winding  (0 if g_c1 > g_c2, else 1).  Therefore

  \[Gamma]_Zak = \[Pi] (w_h - w_C)   (mod 2\[Pi])   \[Element]  {0, \[Pi]} .

It is quantised, and w_h -- hence the whole invariant -- is controlled by \
omega_r through \[CapitalDelta](k) = w_alpha(k) - w_beta(k) - omega_r .\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.997811635752886*^9, 
  3.997811637407151*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"6b2a04fb-690b-4900-9541-\
83826de6392c"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
(* SSH winding: delta_{C,k} = g_c1 + g_c2 e^{-I k} traces a circle of radius \
g_c2 about g_c1 *)
wCwind[gc1_, gc2_] := If[gc2 > gc1, 1, 0];

(* discrete winding of a closed list of complex numbers about the origin *)
windingOf[zs_] := Round[Total[Arg[Rest[zs]/Most[zs]]]/(2 Pi)];

zakTLS[gc1_, gc2_, gJ1_, gJ2_, wrv_, gamv_, nk_: 4000] := Module[
  {ks, dCk, phk, adk, dJk, rhok, delk, zTLS, wH, wC},
  ks   = N@Subdivide[0, 2 Pi, nk];
  dCk  = gc1 + gc2 Exp[-I ks];
  phk  = Arg[dCk];  adk = Abs[dCk];  dJk = gJ1 + gJ2 Exp[-I ks];
  rhok = (1 - 4 adk^2)^(1/4) Im[dJk Exp[-I phk]];
  delk = Sqrt[1 + 2 adk] - Sqrt[1 - 2 adk] - wrv;
  zTLS = gamv rhok + I delk/2;                (* (gam rho, Delta/2) as a \
complex number *)
  wH   = Abs @ windingOf[zTLS];
  wC   = wCwind[gc1, gc2];
  <|\"w_h\" -> wH, \"w_C\" -> wC, \"gammaZak/Pi\" -> Mod[wH - wC, 2]|>];

zakTLS[0.18, 0.11, 1.0, -0.5, 0.30, 0.03]\
\>", "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[108]:=",ExpressionUUID->"5e920a7b-f1a2-48ee-a667-8dc27f46faa8"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"\[LeftAssociation]", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"\<\"w_h\"\>", "\[Rule]", "1"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"\<\"w_C\"\>", "\[Rule]", "0"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"\<\"gammaZak/Pi\"\>", "\[Rule]", "1"}]}], 
  "\[RightAssociation]"}]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.997811436649778*^9},
 CellLabel->
  "Out[116]=",ExpressionUUID->"7eac3d47-9b2c-475a-b223-ac9b6ba678f1"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["8.4  Cross-check against PeriodicChainSW.dressed_zak_phase", \
"Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"e1e534c3-bb92-46db-a5b7-0e8d24b92655"],

Cell["\<\
The quantised TLS prediction is compared with  \
PeriodicChainSW.dressed_zak_phase(band = 1) , the full cavity-dressed \
per-momentum Zak phase of the lower hybridised band (numpy, photon cutoff 6, \
N = 8 chain).  The reference values below were produced by that method; only \
|\[Gamma]_Zak|/\[Pi] (0 vs 1) is physically meaningful.  Points span both \
dimerisation sides and cross the k = 0 interband resonance  omega_r \
\[TildeTilde] Sqrt[1 + 2 ad_0] - Sqrt[1 - 2 ad_0] .\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"d6a6ceae-f9bf-4046-a0ed-95be4202e1de"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
zakReference = {
  <|\"gc1\" -> 0.18, \"gc2\" -> 0.11, \"gJ1\" -> 1.0, \"gJ2\" -> -0.5, \"wr\" \
-> 0.30, \"gam\" -> 0.03, \"dressed\" -> 1|>,
  <|\"gc1\" -> 0.18, \"gc2\" -> 0.11, \"gJ1\" -> 1.0, \"gJ2\" -> -0.5, \"wr\" \
-> 0.55, \"gam\" -> 0.03, \"dressed\" -> 1|>,
  <|\"gc1\" -> 0.18, \"gc2\" -> 0.11, \"gJ1\" -> 1.0, \"gJ2\" -> -0.5, \"wr\" \
-> 0.80, \"gam\" -> 0.03, \"dressed\" -> 0|>,
  <|\"gc1\" -> 0.11, \"gc2\" -> 0.18, \"gJ1\" -> 1.0, \"gJ2\" -> -0.5, \"wr\" \
-> 0.30, \"gam\" -> 0.03, \"dressed\" -> 0|>,
  <|\"gc1\" -> 0.11, \"gc2\" -> 0.18, \"gJ1\" -> 1.0, \"gJ2\" -> -0.5, \"wr\" \
-> 0.80, \"gam\" -> 0.03, \"dressed\" -> 1|>,
  <|\"gc1\" -> 0.18, \"gc2\" -> 0.11, \"gJ1\" -> 1.0, \"gJ2\" -> -0.5, \"wr\" \
-> 0.30, \"gam\" -> 0.06, \"dressed\" -> 1|>,
  <|\"gc1\" -> 0.18, \"gc2\" -> 0.11, \"gJ1\" -> 1.0, \"gJ2\" -> -0.5, \"wr\" \
-> 0.80, \"gam\" -> 0.06, \"dressed\" -> 0|>};

Grid[Prepend[
  Table[Module[{r = zakReference[[i]], z},
     z = zakTLS[r[\"gc1\"], r[\"gc2\"], r[\"gJ1\"], r[\"gJ2\"], r[\"wr\"], r[\
\"gam\"]];
     {i,
      Row[{\"g_c=(\", r[\"gc1\"], \",\", r[\"gc2\"], \")  \",
           If[r[\"gc1\"] > r[\"gc2\"], \"trivial\", \"topological\"],
           \"  omega_r=\", r[\"wr\"], \"  gamma=\", r[\"gam\"]}],
      z[\"w_h\"], z[\"w_C\"], z[\"gammaZak/Pi\"], r[\"dressed\"],
      If[z[\"gammaZak/Pi\"] === r[\"dressed\"], \"\[Checkmark]\", \
\"\[Times]\"]}],
    {i, Length[zakReference]}],
  {\"#\", \"parameters\", \"w_h\", \"w_C\", \"|\[Gamma]_Zak|/\[Pi] (TLS)\",
   \"dressed_zak_phase(1)/\[Pi]\", \"\"}],
 Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]\
\>", "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[117]:=",ExpressionUUID->"d0a26e16-eecc-47ff-af41-2341885b0c6b"],

Cell[BoxData[
 TagBox[GridBox[{
    {"\<\"#\"\>", "\<\"parameters\"\>", "\<\"w_h\"\>", "\<\"w_C\"\>", "\<\"|\
\[Gamma]_Zak|/\[Pi] (TLS)\"\>", "\<\"dressed_zak_phase(1)/\[Pi]\"\>", "\<\"\"\
\>"},
    {"1", 
     TemplateBox[{
      "\"g_c=(\"", "0.18`", "\",\"", "0.11`", "\")  \"", "\"trivial\"", 
       "\"  omega_r=\"", "0.3`", "\"  gamma=\"", "0.03`"},
      "RowDefault"], "1", "0", "1", "1", "\<\"\[Checkmark]\"\>"},
    {"2", 
     TemplateBox[{
      "\"g_c=(\"", "0.18`", "\",\"", "0.11`", "\")  \"", "\"trivial\"", 
       "\"  omega_r=\"", "0.55`", "\"  gamma=\"", "0.03`"},
      "RowDefault"], "1", "0", "1", "1", "\<\"\[Checkmark]\"\>"},
    {"3", 
     TemplateBox[{
      "\"g_c=(\"", "0.18`", "\",\"", "0.11`", "\")  \"", "\"trivial\"", 
       "\"  omega_r=\"", "0.8`", "\"  gamma=\"", "0.03`"},
      "RowDefault"], "0", "0", "0", "0", "\<\"\[Checkmark]\"\>"},
    {"4", 
     TemplateBox[{
      "\"g_c=(\"", "0.11`", "\",\"", "0.18`", "\")  \"", "\"topological\"", 
       "\"  omega_r=\"", "0.3`", "\"  gamma=\"", "0.03`"},
      "RowDefault"], "1", "1", "0", "0", "\<\"\[Checkmark]\"\>"},
    {"5", 
     TemplateBox[{
      "\"g_c=(\"", "0.11`", "\",\"", "0.18`", "\")  \"", "\"topological\"", 
       "\"  omega_r=\"", "0.8`", "\"  gamma=\"", "0.03`"},
      "RowDefault"], "0", "1", "1", "1", "\<\"\[Checkmark]\"\>"},
    {"6", 
     TemplateBox[{
      "\"g_c=(\"", "0.18`", "\",\"", "0.11`", "\")  \"", "\"trivial\"", 
       "\"  omega_r=\"", "0.3`", "\"  gamma=\"", "0.06`"},
      "RowDefault"], "1", "0", "1", "1", "\<\"\[Checkmark]\"\>"},
    {"7", 
     TemplateBox[{
      "\"g_c=(\"", "0.18`", "\",\"", "0.11`", "\")  \"", "\"trivial\"", 
       "\"  omega_r=\"", "0.8`", "\"  gamma=\"", "0.06`"},
      "RowDefault"], "0", "0", "0", "0", "\<\"\[Checkmark]\"\>"}
   },
   AutoDelete->False,
   GridBoxAlignment->{"Columns" -> {{Left}}},
   GridBoxFrame->{"Columns" -> {{True}}, "Rows" -> {{True}}},
   GridBoxItemSize->{"Columns" -> {{Automatic}}, "Rows" -> {{Automatic}}}],
  "Grid"]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.9978114366970463`*^9},
 CellLabel->
  "Out[119]=",ExpressionUUID->"2cc20682-6490-4728-bfeb-4bcfe0be19e2"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell["\<\
The cavity as a topological knob.  At fixed SSH dimerisation w_C, sweeping \
omega_r shifts \[CapitalDelta](k) = w_alpha(k) - w_beta(k) - omega_r rigidly. \
 While omega_r lies inside the band-splitting window  [min_k (w_alpha - \
w_beta), max_k (w_alpha - w_beta)]  the gap \[CapitalDelta](k) changes sign \
somewhere in the BZ, the planar vector (gam rho, \[CapitalDelta]/2) encircles \
the origin (w_h = 1) and \[Gamma]_Zak = \[Pi](1 - w_C).  Once omega_r leaves \
that window \[CapitalDelta](k) keeps one sign, w_h = 0 and \[Gamma]_Zak = -\
\[Pi] w_C.  So the resonator flips the Zak phase by \[Pi] on entering / \
leaving the interband resonance, independent of gamma (which only sets how \
wide the transition region in omega_r is).\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"14be58e4-4c66-459f-84a1-f67471a9a6bc"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["9  Analytical Zak phase of the hybridised band, step by step", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"bfdc495e-e187-4af8-9700-c602790a8f81"],

Cell["\<\
Everything is now an explicit function of k.  We build, in order:  (1) the \
analytic band energies,  (2) the analytic spinors (SSH Bloch spinor \
\[CircleTimes] planar two-level eigenvector, in a periodic gauge),  (3) their \
k-derivatives,  (4) the Berry connection integrand  \[ScriptCapitalA](k) = i \
\[LeftAngleBracket]\[Psi]_k| \[PartialD]_k |\[Psi]_k\[RightAngleBracket]  \
split into blocks,  (5) the block integrals, giving  \[Gamma]_Zak = -\[Pi] \
w_C - \[Pi] w_h \[Congruent] \[Pi] (w_h - w_C).\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"380cd592-18b4-452e-abf8-5320fee5ae84"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["9.1  k-explicit quantities", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"02079b24-cb69-4541-ad49-037b4300857a"],

Cell["\<\
Working symbols:  gc1, gc2 > 0 with gc1 + gc2 < 1/2  (capacitive intra / \
inter hopping);  gJ1, gJ2 real  (Josephson intra / inter);  \[Gamma] > 0  \
(cavity coupling);  \[Omega]r > 0  (cavity frequency).  \[Delta]_(C,k) = gc1 \
+ gc2 e^{-i k},  \[Delta]_(J,k) = gJ1 + gJ2 e^{-i k}.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"30d0fcd3-4f1b-4a2e-8859-22816ded4e84"],

Cell["\<\
$Assumptions = gc1 > 0 && gc2 > 0 && gc1 + gc2 < 1/2 && gJ1 \[Element] Reals &&
   gJ2 \[Element] Reals && \[Gamma] > 0 && \[Omega]r > 0 && k \[Element] Reals;

\[Delta]C[k_] := gc1 + gc2 Exp[-I k];
\[Delta]J[k_] := gJ1 + gJ2 Exp[-I k];
\[Kappa][k_]    := Sqrt[gc1^2 + gc2^2 + 2 gc1 gc2 Cos[k]];        (* \
|\[Delta]_{C,k}| *)
\[CurlyPhi][k_] := ArcTan[gc1 + gc2 Cos[k], -gc2 Sin[k]];        (* arg \
\[Delta]_{C,k}  (two-argument ArcTan) *)

Simplify[{\[Kappa][k]^2 - \[Delta]C[k] Conjugate[\[Delta]C[k]],
          \[Kappa][k] Exp[I \[CurlyPhi][k]] - \[Delta]C[k]}]        (* {0, 0} \
*)\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"cbc165b5-4a09-4194-90e4-d7e60d286519"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["9.2  Analytical energies", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"33ed992d-f07e-463c-bf09-4e0cc8a73ee7"],

Cell["\<\
The capacitive bands are  \[Omega]\[Alpha],\[Beta](k) = Sqrt[1 \[PlusMinus] 2 \
|\[Delta]_{C,k}|]  (section 4).  The doublet {|\[Alpha]_k, 0\
\[RightAngleBracket], |\[Beta]_k, 1\[RightAngleBracket]} has detuning \
\[CapitalDelta](k) = \[Omega]\[Alpha] - \[Omega]\[Beta] - \[Omega]r and is \
coupled by  \[Tilde]A_J[\[Alpha]_k, \[Beta]_k] = i \[Rho](k)  (section 5, \
purely imaginary), with the real amplitude  \[Rho](k) = (1 - \
4|\[Delta]_C|^2)^{1/4} Im[\[Delta]_{J,k} e^{-i\[CurlyPhi]_k}]  which here \
collapses to  (1 - 4|\[Delta]_C|^2)^{1/4} (gc2 gJ1 - gc1 gJ2) Sin[k] / |\
\[Delta]_C| .  The hybridised band energies are  \
\[ScriptCapitalE]\[PlusMinus](k) = (\[Omega]\[Alpha] + \[Omega]\[Beta] + \
\[Omega]r)/2 \[PlusMinus] R(k),  R = Sqrt[(\[Gamma]\[Rho])^2 + (\
\[CapitalDelta]/2)^2].\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"caf8c59a-b419-4279-86f5-3c42f7c928c1"],

Cell["\<\
\[Omega]\[Alpha][k_] := Sqrt[1 + 2 \[Kappa][k]];
\[Omega]\[Beta][k_]  := Sqrt[1 - 2 \[Kappa][k]];
\[CapitalDelta][k_]  := \[Omega]\[Alpha][k] - \[Omega]\[Beta][k] - \[Omega]r;

\[Rho][k_] := (1 - 4 \[Kappa][k]^2)^(1/4)/\[Kappa][k] *
   ComplexExpand[Im[(gJ1 + gJ2 Exp[-I k]) (gc1 + gc2 Exp[I k])]];
Print[\"\[Rho](k) = \", \[Rho][k]];                       (* -> \
(1-4\[Kappa]^2)^(1/4) (gc2 gJ1 - gc1 gJ2) Sin[k] / \[Kappa] *)

R[k_] := Sqrt[(\[Gamma] \[Rho][k])^2 + (\[CapitalDelta][k]/2)^2];
\[ScriptCapitalE]lo[k_] := (\[Omega]\[Alpha][k] + \[Omega]\[Beta][k] + \
\[Omega]r)/2 - R[k];   (* lower hybridised band *)
\[ScriptCapitalE]hi[k_]  := (\[Omega]\[Alpha][k] + \[Omega]\[Beta][k] + \
\[Omega]r)/2 + R[k];
Column[{Row[{\"\[ScriptCapitalE]lo(k) = \", \[ScriptCapitalE]lo[k]}],
        Row[{\"\[ScriptCapitalE]hi(k) = \",  \[ScriptCapitalE]hi[k]}]}]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"35ef2499-1f22-47c8-acf4-bc8e062f1097"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["9.3  Analytical spinors (periodic gauge)", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"c0b172d7-d044-4e43-94fa-dc92ce6af8be"],

Cell["\<\
The planar pseudo-spin is  h(k) = (0, \[Gamma]\[Rho](k), \
\[CapitalDelta](k)/2);  its polar angle is  \[Theta](k) = \
atan2(\[Gamma]\[Rho], \[CapitalDelta]/2).  The lower two-level eigenvector \
c(k) = (i Sin[\[Theta]/2], Cos[\[Theta]/2])  is anti-periodic across the BZ \
whenever \[Theta] winds an odd number of times, so we use the periodic-gauge \
vector  cP(k) = e^{i\[Theta]/2} c(k), which is a function of e^{i\[Theta]} \
alone.  The SSH Bloch spinors are  u\[Alpha],\[Beta](k) = (1, \[PlusMinus] \
e^{-i\[CurlyPhi]_k})/Sqrt[2].  The hybridised chain / photon state, in the \
basis (A,0),(B,0),(A,1),(B,1), is |\[Psi]_k\[RightAngleBracket] = cP_1 |u\
\[Alpha]\[RightAngleBracket]\[TensorProduct]|0\[RightAngleBracket] + cP_2 |u\
\[Beta]\[RightAngleBracket]\[TensorProduct]|1\[RightAngleBracket].\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"36f54ebe-31a8-452b-92d6-45a467842d56"],

Cell["\<\
\[Theta][k_] := ArcTan[\[CapitalDelta][k]/2, \[Gamma] \[Rho][k]];      (* \
polar angle of the planar pseudo-spin *)

eMi\[CurlyPhi][k_] := (gc1 + gc2 Exp[I k])/\[Kappa][k];               (* \
e^{-i \[CurlyPhi]_k} , since k is real *)
u\[Alpha][k_] := {1,  eMi\[CurlyPhi][k]}/Sqrt[2];
u\[Beta][k_]  := {1, -eMi\[CurlyPhi][k]}/Sqrt[2];

c[k_]  := {I Sin[\[Theta][k]/2], Cos[\[Theta][k]/2]};              (* natural \
gauge (anti-periodic) *)
cP[k_] := Exp[I \[Theta][k]/2] c[k];                               (* \
periodic gauge *)
Print[\"cP , as a function of t = \[Theta](k):  \",
      ComplexExpand[Exp[I t/2] {I Sin[t/2], Cos[t/2]}] // Simplify];   (* \
function of Exp[I t] -> periodic *)

\[Psi][k_] := cP[k][[1]] Flatten@KroneckerProduct[u\[Alpha][k], {1, 0}] +
              cP[k][[2]] Flatten@KroneckerProduct[u\[Beta][k],  {0, 1}];

(* structure, with s = Sin[\[Theta]/2], cc = Cos[\[Theta]/2], p = e^{-i\
\[CurlyPhi]} *)
Print[\"|\[Psi]_k\[RightAngleBracket] = cP_1(k) \
|u\[Alpha]\[RightAngleBracket]\[CircleTimes]|0\[RightAngleBracket] + cP_2(k) \
|u\[Beta]\[RightAngleBracket]\[CircleTimes]|1\[RightAngleBracket]  =\"];
Print[MatrixForm[{I s Exp[I th/2]/Sqrt[2], cc Exp[I th/2]/Sqrt[2],
                  I s Exp[I th/2] p/Sqrt[2], -cc Exp[I th/2] p/Sqrt[2]}]];

(* norm is 1 for every k (proven symbolically in section 8 with abstract real \
\[Theta]);
   FullSimplify on the fully-explicit \[Psi] is a memory hog, so here a \
numeric spot check *)
normAt[kv_] := Chop[N[Conjugate[\[Psi][k]] . \[Psi][k] /.
   {gc1 -> 0.18, gc2 -> 0.11, gJ1 -> 1.0, gJ2 -> -0.5, \[Gamma] -> 0.04, \
\[Omega]r -> 0.55, k -> kv}]];
Print[\"\[LeftAngleBracket]\[Psi]_k|\[Psi]_k\[RightAngleBracket] at k = 0.3, \
1.1, 2.4, 4.0 :  \", normAt /@ {0.3, 1.1, 2.4, 4.0}]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"0da183d3-6d5a-4430-84fd-fc2a3a9f21f0"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["9.4  Analytical derivatives", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"9da4faee-2ceb-4dc9-a5a4-b830a40bff2f"],

Cell["\<\
Only two derivatives feed the Berry connection:  \[CurlyPhi]'(k)  (SSH Bloch \
phase) and  \[Theta]'(k)  (pseudo-spin angle).  \[CurlyPhi]'(k)  is \
elementary;  \[Theta]'(k)  is lengthy (LeafCount ~ 400) but explicit -- it is \
only ever used under the BZ integral.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"186a9cd3-0825-42ad-891e-066bb0767623"],

Cell["\<\
\[CurlyPhi]d[k_] = Simplify[D[\[CurlyPhi][k], k]];       (* elementary *)
Print[\"\[CurlyPhi]'(k) = \", \[CurlyPhi]d[k]];        (* -gc2 (gc2 + gc1 \
Cos[k]) / (gc1^2 + gc2^2 + 2 gc1 gc2 Cos[k]) *)

\[Theta]d[k_] = D[\[Theta][k], k];      (* = (X Y' - Y X')/(X^2 + Y^2),  X = \
\[CapitalDelta]/2, Y = \[Gamma]\[Rho];  left raw -- large *)
Print[\"\[Theta]'(k)  LeafCount = \", LeafCount[\[Theta]d[k]], \"   (kept \
unsimplified; only used under the BZ integral / numerically)\"];

\[Psi]d[k_] = D[\[Psi][k], k];          (* 4-vector, raw *)
Print[\"\[PartialD]_k \[Psi]_k  LeafCount = \", LeafCount[\[Psi]d[k]]];
Print[\"\[Theta]'(k) numeric @ \
(gc1,gc2,gJ1,gJ2,\[Gamma],\[Omega]r,k)=(.18,.11,1,-.5,.03,.55,1.0) = \",
      N[\[Theta]d[k] /. {gc1 -> .18, gc2 -> .11, gJ1 -> 1., gJ2 -> -.5, \
\[Gamma] -> .03, \[Omega]r -> .55, k -> 1.0}]]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"f59324e4-7fb0-4fe8-9210-ffa9a280973d"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["9.5  The Berry connection integrand, in blocks", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"d6a15320-6b1c-422d-8b7a-8a4d8785f591"],

Cell["\<\
\[ScriptCapitalA](k) = i \[LeftAngleBracket]\[Psi]_k| \[PartialD]_k |\[Psi]_k\
\[RightAngleBracket].  Two useful splittings.  (a) By physical origin:  the \
SSH Bloch spinors carry the SAME orbital connection \[ScriptCapitalA]_orb^\
\[Alpha] = \[ScriptCapitalA]_orb^\[Beta] = \
i\[LeftAngleBracket]u_s|\[PartialD]_k u_s\[RightAngleBracket] = \
\[CurlyPhi]'/2, and the periodic-gauge pseudo-spinor carries \
\[ScriptCapitalA]_TLS = i\[LeftAngleBracket]cP|\[PartialD]_k cP\
\[RightAngleBracket] = -\[Theta]'/2; since the orbital connections are equal \
they factor out of the |cP|^2-weighted superposition, giving \
\[ScriptCapitalA] = \[ScriptCapitalA]_TLS + \[CurlyPhi]'/2.  (b) By \
sublattice:  the A-sublattice components give -\[Theta]'/4, the B-sublattice \
components (which carry e^{-i\[CurlyPhi]}) give \[CurlyPhi]'/2 - \[Theta]'/4. \
 Both give  \[ScriptCapitalA](k) = \[CurlyPhi]'(k)/2 - \[Theta]'(k)/2.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"cf35fe00-6419-4492-b927-76db8f68c5e7"],

Cell["\<\
(* -- block (a): orbital vs pseudo-spin, shown with abstract real \[Theta], \
\[CurlyPhi] -- *)
With[{U\[Alpha] = {1, Exp[-I \[Phi][k]]}/Sqrt[2], U\[Beta] = {1, -Exp[-I \
\[Phi][k]]}/Sqrt[2],
      CP = Exp[I \[CapitalTheta][k]/2] {I Sin[\[CapitalTheta][k]/2], Cos[\
\[CapitalTheta][k]/2]}},
 Aorb\[Alpha] = ComplexExpand[I Conjugate[U\[Alpha]] . D[U\[Alpha], k]] // \
FullSimplify;
 Aorb\[Beta]  = ComplexExpand[I Conjugate[U\[Beta]]  . D[U\[Beta],  k]] // \
FullSimplify;
 Atls    = ComplexExpand[I Conjugate[CP] . D[CP, k]] // FullSimplify;
 Print[\"\[ScriptCapitalA]_orb^\[Alpha] = \[ScriptCapitalA]_orb^\[Beta] = \", \
{Aorb\[Alpha], Aorb\[Beta]},
       \"   (= \[CurlyPhi]'/2)\"];
 Print[\"\[ScriptCapitalA]_TLS = \", Atls, \"   (= -\[CapitalTheta]'/2)\"];
]

(* -- block (b): by sublattice, and the total, again with abstract \[Theta], \
\[CurlyPhi] -- *)
psiAbstract = With[{U\[Alpha] = {1, Exp[-I \[Phi][k]]}/Sqrt[2], U\[Beta] = \
{1, -Exp[-I \[Phi][k]]}/Sqrt[2],
      CP = Exp[I \[CapitalTheta][k]/2] {I Sin[\[CapitalTheta][k]/2], Cos[\
\[CapitalTheta][k]/2]}},
   CP[[1]] Flatten@KroneckerProduct[U\[Alpha], {1, 0}] + CP[[2]] \
Flatten@KroneckerProduct[U\[Beta], {0, 1}]];
blkA  = ComplexExpand[I Conjugate[psiAbstract[[{1, 2}]]] . D[psiAbstract[[{1, \
2}]], k]] // FullSimplify;
blkB  = ComplexExpand[I Conjugate[psiAbstract[[{3, 4}]]] . D[psiAbstract[[{3, \
4}]], k]] // FullSimplify;
Atot  = ComplexExpand[I Conjugate[psiAbstract] . D[psiAbstract, k]] // \
FullSimplify;
Print[\"sublattice A block  = \", blkA];
Print[\"sublattice B block  = \", blkB];
Print[\"\[ScriptCapitalA](k)          = \", Atot,
      \"     ( \[CurlyPhi]'/2 - \[CapitalTheta]'/2 ,  check -> \",
      FullSimplify[Atot - (Derivative[1][\[Phi]][k]/2 - Derivative[1][\
\[CapitalTheta]][k]/2)], \" )\"];

(* -- plug in the explicit k-dependence -- *)
integrand[k_] = \[CurlyPhi]d[k]/2 - \[Theta]d[k]/2;
Print[\"integrand(k) = \[CurlyPhi]'(k)/2 - \[Theta]'(k)/2 ,  LeafCount = \", \
LeafCount[integrand[k]]];\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"c0e98555-b665-4f88-b4f0-5cb90434f5c6"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["9.6  The two block integrals", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"67668e48-a330-42d8-a1f7-495adec66978"],

Cell["\<\
\[Gamma]_Zak = \[Integral]_0^{2\[Pi]} \[ScriptCapitalA](k) dk  =  \[Integral] \
\[CurlyPhi]'/2 dk  -  \[Integral] \[Theta]'/2 dk.  The orbital block \
integrates in closed form to  -\[Pi] w_C  (w_C = 0 if gc1 > gc2, else 1 -- \
the SSH winding).  The pseudo-spin block is a winding number: \[Integral] \
\[Theta]'(k) dk = 2\[Pi] w_h  with  w_h  the number of times  \
(\[Gamma]\[Rho](k), \[CapitalDelta](k)/2)  circles the origin;  Integrate \
cannot resolve this for generic parameters, so w_h is read off numerically.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"3a3f3c7d-4001-4e9b-a30e-30cb59c5b767"],

Cell["\<\
(* orbital block -- exact, symbolic *)
orbitalTrivial     = Assuming[gc1 > gc2 > 0, Integrate[\[CurlyPhi]d[k]/2, {k, \
0, 2 Pi}]];   (* 0    -> w_C = 0 *)
orbitalTopological = Assuming[gc2 > gc1 > 0, Integrate[\[CurlyPhi]d[k]/2, {k, \
0, 2 Pi}]];   (* -\[Pi]  -> w_C = 1 *)
Print[\"\[Integral] \[CurlyPhi]'/2 dk  =  -\[Pi] w_C :   gc1>gc2 -> \", \
orbitalTrivial,
      \" ;   gc2>gc1 -> \", orbitalTopological];

(* pseudo-spin block -- winding number of (\[Gamma]\[Rho], \[CapitalDelta]/2) \
about the origin *)
windingOf[z_] := Round[Total[Arg[Rest[z]/Most[z]]] / (2 Pi)];
wHof[gc1v_, gc2v_, gJ1v_, gJ2v_, \[Gamma]v_, \[Omega]rv_, nk_: 4000] := Module[
  {g, \[Kappa]n, \[CurlyPhi]n, \[Rho]n, \[CapitalDelta]n},
  g = N@Subdivide[0, 2 Pi, nk];
  \[Kappa]n = Sqrt[gc1v^2 + gc2v^2 + 2 gc1v gc2v Cos[g]];
  \[CurlyPhi]n = Arg[gc1v + gc2v Exp[-I g]];
  \[Rho]n = (1 - 4 \[Kappa]n^2)^(1/4) Im[(gJ1v + gJ2v Exp[-I g]) Exp[-I \
\[CurlyPhi]n]];
  \[CapitalDelta]n = Sqrt[1 + 2 \[Kappa]n] - Sqrt[1 - 2 \[Kappa]n] - \
\[Omega]rv;
  Abs @ windingOf[\[Gamma]v \[Rho]n + I \[CapitalDelta]n/2]];
Print[\"example  w_h(gc1=.18, gc2=.11, gJ1=1, gJ2=-.5, \[Gamma]=.03, \
\[Omega]r=.55) = \",
      wHof[0.18, 0.11, 1.0, -0.5, 0.03, 0.55]];\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"ee86ae0e-01a7-4bb9-a514-ed573756792e"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["9.7  \[Gamma]_Zak assembled, and cross-check vs PeriodicChainSW", \
"Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"299c715b-3da6-4b38-ab48-19b4c6d85247"],

Cell["\<\
\[Gamma]_Zak = -\[Pi] w_C - \[Pi] w_h  \[Congruent]  \[Pi] (w_h - w_C)  (mod \
2\[Pi])  \[Element] {0, \[Pi]} -- quantised, with the cavity frequency \
\[Omega]r entering only through w_h.  Checked against the fully \
cavity-dressed Wilson-loop Zak phase  PeriodicChainSW.dressed_zak_phase(1)  \
(numpy, photon cutoff 6, N = 8), for which |\[Gamma]_Zak|/\[Pi] is the \
physical (0 vs 1) content.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"aabc96a8-859b-4129-97f4-a22c2278bee8"],

Cell["\<\
zakReference = {
  <|\"gc1\"->0.18,\"gc2\"->0.11,\"gJ1\"->1.0,\"gJ2\"->-0.5,\"\[Gamma]\"->0.03,\
\"\[Omega]r\"->0.30,\"dressed\"->1|>,
  <|\"gc1\"->0.18,\"gc2\"->0.11,\"gJ1\"->1.0,\"gJ2\"->-0.5,\"\[Gamma]\"->0.03,\
\"\[Omega]r\"->0.55,\"dressed\"->1|>,
  <|\"gc1\"->0.18,\"gc2\"->0.11,\"gJ1\"->1.0,\"gJ2\"->-0.5,\"\[Gamma]\"->0.03,\
\"\[Omega]r\"->0.80,\"dressed\"->0|>,
  <|\"gc1\"->0.11,\"gc2\"->0.18,\"gJ1\"->1.0,\"gJ2\"->-0.5,\"\[Gamma]\"->0.03,\
\"\[Omega]r\"->0.30,\"dressed\"->0|>,
  <|\"gc1\"->0.11,\"gc2\"->0.18,\"gJ1\"->1.0,\"gJ2\"->-0.5,\"\[Gamma]\"->0.03,\
\"\[Omega]r\"->0.80,\"dressed\"->1|>,
  <|\"gc1\"->0.18,\"gc2\"->0.11,\"gJ1\"->1.0,\"gJ2\"->-0.5,\"\[Gamma]\"->0.06,\
\"\[Omega]r\"->0.30,\"dressed\"->1|>,
  <|\"gc1\"->0.18,\"gc2\"->0.11,\"gJ1\"->1.0,\"gJ2\"->-0.5,\"\[Gamma]\"->0.06,\
\"\[Omega]r\"->0.80,\"dressed\"->0|>};

zakFromBlocks[p_] := Module[{wC, wh},
  wC = If[p[\"gc1\"] > p[\"gc2\"], 0, 1];
  wh = wHof[p[\"gc1\"], p[\"gc2\"], p[\"gJ1\"], p[\"gJ2\"], p[\"\[Gamma]\"], \
p[\"\[Omega]r\"]];
  <|\"w_C\" -> wC, \"w_h\" -> wh, \"\[Gamma]Zak/\[Pi]\" -> Mod[wh - wC, 2]|>];

Grid[Prepend[
  Table[Module[{p = zakReference[[i]], b},
     b = zakFromBlocks[p];
     {i, Row[{\"g_c=(\", p[\"gc1\"], \",\", p[\"gc2\"], \")  \",
              If[p[\"gc1\"] > p[\"gc2\"], \"trivial\", \"topological\"],
              \"  \[Omega]r=\", p[\"\[Omega]r\"], \"  \[Gamma]=\", p[\"\
\[Gamma]\"]}],
      b[\"w_C\"], b[\"w_h\"], b[\"\[Gamma]Zak/\[Pi]\"], p[\"dressed\"],
      If[b[\"\[Gamma]Zak/\[Pi]\"] === p[\"dressed\"], \"\[Checkmark]\", \"\
\[Times]\"]}],
    {i, Length[zakReference]}],
  {\"#\", \"parameters\", \"w_C\", \"w_h\", \"|\[Gamma]_Zak|/\[Pi]\", \
\"dressed_zak_phase(1)/\[Pi]\", \"\"}],
 Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"e0f31617-4238-47cb-93b9-df2395c01552"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell["\<\
The cavity as a topological knob.  w_C is fixed by the SSH dimerisation.  \
\[Omega]r shifts \[CapitalDelta](k) = \[Omega]\[Alpha](k) - \
\[Omega]\[Beta](k) - \[Omega]r rigidly:  while \[Omega]r lies inside the \
interband-splitting window  [min_k(\[Omega]\[Alpha]-\[Omega]\[Beta]), max_k(\
\[Omega]\[Alpha]-\[Omega]\[Beta])]  the detuning changes sign in the BZ, the \
planar vector (\[Gamma]\[Rho], \[CapitalDelta]/2) encircles the origin, w_h = \
1 and \[Gamma]_Zak = \[Pi](1 - w_C); outside the window w_h = 0 and \
\[Gamma]_Zak = -\[Pi] w_C.  So the resonator toggles the Zak phase by \[Pi] \
on crossing the interband resonance, independent of \[Gamma] (which only sets \
how sharp the transition in \[Omega]r is).\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"32947002-756d-4e24-93db-051bbdf600fd"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]]
},
WindowSize->{1440, 750.75},
WindowMargins->{{0, Automatic}, {Automatic, 0}},
